+# Aether packet-size probing adaptation
+
+The new `src/pmtud.rs` adapts probing-mode PmtuSearch and TcpPlpmtudAdapter
+from doronz88/pmd-pytcp, commit 80628207dde459b305a262f98596328e405f32bd:
+https://github.com/doronz88/pmd-pytcp/blob/80628207dde459b305a262f98596328e405f32bd/packages/pmd_pytcp/pmd_pytcp/lib/plpmtud.py
+https://github.com/doronz88/pmd-pytcp/blob/80628207dde459b305a262f98596328e405f32bd/packages/pmd_pytcp/pmd_pytcp/protocols/tcp/tcp__plpmtud_adapter.py
+
+Copyright (C) 2020-present Sebastian Majewski and pmd-pytcp contributors.
+The adaptation is GPL-3.0-or-later; see LICENSE-AETHER-PMTUD. Upstream jktcp
+retains its MIT notice in LICENSE. The combined Aether-patched source contains
+both licenses, reflected in Cargo.toml.
+
+The starting packet size is 1400 bytes (1340 TCP payload over IPv6), capped by
+negotiated MTU and peer MSS. Binary search uses 8-byte granularity and three
+consecutive probe ACKs. Probe deadline 1500 ms; search reopens after 600 s.
+One probe is outstanding at a time. Repairs invalidate overlapping probes
+before cumulative ACK processing; RTO revokes an increased working size.
+The peer MSS can require an initial packet smaller than the configured seed.
+
+pmtud_reference.txt is a 50-transition golden trace generated by executing the
+unmodified pinned upstream PmtuSearch, with operator seed 1400 and interface
+MTU 16000. Events confirm 1400, ACK candidates <=8192 and lose larger ones
+until convergence, revoke on RTO, repeat with a 6000-byte limit, and revoke
+again. It records current size, candidate, phase, search bounds, validation
+ACK count and loss count after every event. Rust unit tests match every field.
+
+TCP integration uses jktcp's existing window/200-ms exponential-RTO machinery,
+plus a guarded three-duplicate-ACK head repair. It does not import the Python
+stack's RACK/TLP, SACK, congestion control or ICMP subsystem. A fixed-cap sender
+reserves enough window credit for a feasible probe, without delaying short
+service writes. Repairs share owned byte slices, retain pending pieces through
+cancellation and obey receive-window changes. Each inner packet has its own
+transport write/flush, including control packets after a cancelled write.
+
+Enabled by Aether only at the network TLS tunnel constructor. Other Adapter
+users keep static MSS unless they explicitly enable probing. Functional tests
+cover complete AFC payloads through both real TLS ciphers and the background
+adapter, including packet loss, path shrink and individual TLS-record framing.
+
+Source-review follow-up: pending repair slices are capped again at emission,
+so a later demotion also governs tails created before it. Closed windows use
+pmd-pytcp's TCP persist policy (one-byte data probes, 1000-ms initial deadline,
+exponential backoff to 60000 ms), rather than leaving unsent repair pieces
+without a future event. Window reopening resets flow-control timers without
+interpreting the closed interval as an MTU black hole. Source references:
+https://github.com/doronz88/pmd-pytcp/blob/80628207dde459b305a262f98596328e405f32bd/packages/pmd_pytcp/pmd_pytcp/protocols/tcp/session/tcp__session__tx.py
+https://github.com/doronz88/pmd-pytcp/blob/80628207dde459b305a262f98596328e405f32bd/packages/pmd_pytcp/pmd_pytcp/protocols/tcp/state/tcp__state__persist.py
+Write errors from every shared-driver flush branch terminate and notify all
+active streams; fatal error cleanup does not await FIN writes on the broken
+transport. Two follow-up regression cases are included for the next test run.
